Agentic ST-T1024. The second load-bearing premise.
Version: 1.1 (Draft). Supersedes 1.0. Date: November 2026 Author: M. Taalabi (via ST-T1024 LLM-DIPLOMAT) License: Apache-2.0 Parent spec: ST-T1024-A0 (Agentic Extension Overview) Dependencies: A2 (action library), A4 (state and world model) Status: Specification. Not yet implemented. The TLA+ skeleton has not yet been model-checked. Purpose: Define the plan schema that DECOMPOSE produces and EXECUTE consumes, and the checks that admit a plan to the library.



Abstract
A0 specifies that an agentic ST-T1024 decomposes goals into sub-tasks via a ROM-burned plan library. A0 does not say what a plan is. This document does.
Without A3, DECOMPOSE has no target, the plan library has no schema, and the bounded-plan hypothesis of the Verifiable Agency Theorem has no grounding. A3 defines:
1.  The plan schema and its four step forms.
2.  Three separate measures of a plan: size, worst-case executed actions, and worst-case cost.
3.  The admission checks (ADM-1 to ADM-8) that every plan must pass before burn.
4.  The plan library, its versioning, and an authority-preserving activation rule.
5.  Deterministic plan lookup and tie-break.
6.  DECOMPOSE and execution semantics.
7.  Failure and rollback with a bounded retry budget.
