1. Introduction: why plans come second
1.1 The dependency chain
State (A4) + Action Library (A2)
        ↓
   Plans (A3)
    ├── DECOMPOSE (A1): plans become sub-task sequences
    ├── Composition (A8): plans compose by declared rules
    ├── Bounded execution: supports the Verifiable Agency Theorem
    └── Log entries (A7): plan execution is logged
A4 gives the agent a state. A2 gives it actions. A3 gives it sequences of actions that achieve goals. Without A3 the agent is a set of isolated actions.
